  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">A sculptural book by SCAD Fibers student Claire Masters. The book is reminiscent of a dandelion parachute ball. Masters used rice paper, pins, foam, and an inkjet printer in the work, which is supported in a glass bottle. The book is interactive: readers can remove a pin to read the message printed there. Masters' book won third place in ACA Library's 2nd Annual Student Artists' Book Competion, jurored by Dayna Thacker.</subfield>
